{"id": "unknown-2026-05-23-019", "date": "2026-05-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Charging ahead: Kuala Lumpur, Penang beat EVSE deployment goals", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/05/Kuala_Lumpur_skyline.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>While some nations and their Boomer leaders cling to some imagined past, the rest of the world is charging towards a zero-emission future. Now, you can add Malaysian states Kuala Lumpur and Penang to the latter list, as <em>both</em> states exceeded their annual EV charger deployment goal … and they did it in March!</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-la", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/05/23/charging-ahead-kuala-lumpur-penang-beat-evse-deployment-goals/", "type": "rss"}]}
